      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.689,
            0.048,
            0.86,
            0.066
          ],
          "content": "Fractions in Disguise"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.089,
            0.258,
            0.11
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "A Mishap"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.124,
            0.847,
            0.2
          ],
          "content": "？ **Example 13:** After Surbhi bought cookware from the wholesaler, she kept a profit margin of 50% on all the products. To clear off the remaining stock, she thought she would offer a 50% discount and come out without any loss."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.204,
            0.584,
            0.224
          ],
          "content": "(i) Do you think she didn’t make any loss?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.158,
            0.227,
            0.846,
            0.266
          ],
          "content": "(ii) If she had sold goods (originally) for ₹12,000 after discount, how much loss did she incur? What is the percentage loss?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.27,
            0.847,
            0.325
          ],
          "content": "(iii) What should have been the percentage discount offered so that she sold the goods at the price she had bought (i.e., no profit or loss)?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.332,
            0.459,
            0.351
          ],
          "content": "Let us model the situation first."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.351,
            0.538,
            0.389
          ],
          "content": "Suppose the worth of the products she bought from the wholesaler is x."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.389,
            0.538,
            0.425
          ],
          "content": "The worth corresponding to the selling price (with a 50% margin) is 1.5x."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.424,
            0.538,
            0.462
          ],
          "content": "make the worth 0.75x."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.552,
            0.322,
            0.927,
            0.461
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_26_image_10.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.156,
            0.472,
            0.847,
            0.512
          ],
          "content": "(i) This means the selling price is $\\frac { 3 } { 4 }$ of the price the goods were bought at, i.e., a 25% loss."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.515,
            0.556,
            0.536
          ],
          "content": "(ii) If she had sold goods worth ₹12,000,"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.427,
            0.539,
            0.571,
            0.56
          ],
          "content": "0.75x = 12,000",
          "image_source": "images/page_26_equation_13.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.444,
            0.569,
            0.553,
            0.59
          ],
          "content": "x = 16, 000.",
          "image_source": "images/page_26_equation_14.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.199,
            0.594,
            0.347,
            0.612
          ],
          "content": "She lost ₹4000."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.617,
            0.836,
            0.638
          ],
          "content": "(iii) To sell the goods at the same price, the discount offered should be"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.406,
            0.642,
            0.594,
            0.661
          ],
          "content": "1.5x - d \\times (1.5x) = x",
          "image_source": "images/page_26_equation_17.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.439,
            0.673,
            0.558,
            0.699
          ],
          "content": "d = { \\frac { 1 } { 3 } } = 0 . 3 3 .",
          "image_source": "images/page_26_equation_18.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.197,
            0.702,
            0.657,
            0.722
          ],
          "content": "The discount offered should have been 33.33%."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.732,
            0.811,
            0.809
          ],
          "content": "？ Ariba and Arun have some marbles. Ariba says, “The number of marbles with me is 120% of the marbles Arun has”. What would be an appropriate statement Arun could make comparing the number of marbles he has with Ariba’s?"
        },
        {
